 "notes": "The three cabled ports (mini-HDMI at x = 12.4, micro-USB data at 41.4, power at 54.0) are all on the same long edge (-Y); the microSD slot is on the -X short edge; since generalize delta 002 D1 it is the connector 'sd', which mates card_microsd (the card plus its fingertip access zone, the same section as sd_card_zone), so a text naming a microSD card exposes it like a cable port. The GPIO footprint (PINS_A / PINS_B, 20 positions, rows 2.54 mm apart) is unpopulated on a plain Zero 2 W; a stacked hat (design G07) sits ABOVE the board on header_female_2p54, so no 'mount' stack block is given here (the layout 'mount' mechanism lifts the module on headers under the PCB, which is the Pico 2 case, not this one); the hat's header base is PCB_TOP at z = pcb_thickness and the pins point +Z. HDMI to USB spacing (29 mm) leaves room for the two overmolds (about 17 and 10 mm wide). The HDMI centre x and the USB centres are measured from the SD short edge in the mechanical drawing. Import gate: R1 PCB 65 x 30; R2 hole pitch 58 x 23 and diameter 2.75; R3 axes -Y/-X; R4 overhangs assumed (tol 0.5); R9 skipped.",
